incident :the_sanchakou_ring do
  name "The Sanchakou Ring"
  tags :ecology, :catastrophe, :prediction, :agriculture
  prominence :marginal

  prose <<~PROSE
    Compartment Twelve at #{ref :tangwang_post, "Tangwang Post"}: two hectares of larch and birch on the Tangwang's east bank, with four apple-pear rows and a hazel coppice at its south corner belonging to #{ref :sanchakou, "Sanchakou"}. #{ref :continuity, "Continuity"}'s cabinet marked the forest as changing on 14 September 2089, after nine readings of altered weather and animal movement.

    Two of #{ref :xie_lanting, "Xie Lanting"}'s twenty cores contained closed sleeves of foreign tissue, below the reach threshold of four, in September and again at bud-break. #{ref :nadya_tsoi, "Nadya Tsoi"} walked the compartment on the thirtieth of May in #{year :now} CE and marked it two days later. The ring closed on the twelfth of June: 2,914 stems, nine crew, one hammer, between 04:12 and 20:40.
  PROSE

  prose <<~PROSE, section: :course, heading: "Eleven Days"
    The two-kilometre belt behind the new ring put Sanchakou 1,600 metres inside dead ground. The settlement's thirty-one households moved south along the same road in the eleven days between Nadya's mark and the first cut. The clinic, work crews and neighbouring households moved together; the graves did not.

    The crew worked the north edge inward. Every stem over 40 millimetres took a ring at 1.3 metres, packed with lime-and-oil paste and struck with the number above the cut; smaller stems were cut at the collar and the faces painted. The number is what will separate these stems from the ones #{ref :the_others, "the Others"} kill in the same ground. The tally closed at 2,914 against the hammer count and the crew came out through the apple-pear rows at the south corner.
  PROSE

  prose <<~PROSE, section: :aftermath, heading: "Sixty Sticks"
    Xie had cut the orchard's scionwood in March, dormant: sixty sticks off the four rows, grafted onto rootstock in the post's nursery bed in April and carried to the new row's ground with the households. The cabinet objected when the wood left the compartment. Tsoi let it pass.

    Sanchakou asked to move the graves with the houses. The line service left them because a shovelful of soil can carry the same foreign tissue the ring was cut to contain. The rise stands two hundred and fifty metres behind the ring line, and family members reach it with the coring team four times a year.

    Forty-three of the sixty grafts were in leaf by the second week after the move. The old trees were grey by the next summer.
  PROSE
end
